* The conductor bridge: the primitive character ` Y = N DChrPrim X ` is primitive modulo ` M = N DChrCond X ` , and ` M = 1 ` exactly when ` X ` is principal.

s1::dchrcondnn |- ( ( N e. NN /\ X e. ( Base ` ( DChr ` N ) ) ) -> ( N DChrCond X ) e. NN )
s2::dchrprimcl |- ( ( N e. NN /\ X e. ( Base ` ( DChr ` N ) ) ) -> ( N DChrPrim X ) e. ( Base ` ( DChr ` ( N DChrCond X ) ) ) )
